  "summaries": {
    "en": "Wirebird mechanics, Silkbind attacks, Rampage quest strategy, and Sunbreak endgame preparation for Monster Hunter Rise.",
    "ja": "翔蟲アクション、鉄蟲糸技、百竜夜行戦略、サンブレイク終盤準備まで解説するモンスターハンターライズ攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "action-rpg",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542751371-adc38448a05e?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Wiredash mobility is the most powerful traversal tool in Rise—maintain two Wirebug charges in reserve during combat for emergency repositioning and recovery from knockdowns, not just for Silkbind attacks.",
      "Silkbind attacks have unique properties beyond damage: some apply status (Silkbind Spinning Bludgeon paralyzes), some provide damage buff windows (Switch Axe Silkbind Shade), and some trigger special mechanics on monsters (Heavy Bowgun Wyvern Counter). Learn your weapon's Silkbind functions before optimising combos.",
      "Rampage quests scale in difficulty with the size of your Hunter Rank—complete Rampage quests with at least one Artillery installation and two Melee installations pre-placed at wave start to maximise automated damage.",
      "In Sunbreak, Anomaly Research Points gate endgame crafting—prioritise A-Rank Anomaly quests (unlocked at AR 21) over standard quests once available, as the drop rate for Afflicted materials is 3× higher than standard Anomaly quests.",
      "The Palamute is effectively a second hunter—equip Palamute with Nulberries, Max Potions, and Dango Tickets via the buddy armour screen to provide passive healing and status clearing during hunts."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "翔蟲疾走は最も強力な移動手段。翔蟲チャージを2個、戦闘中の緊急離脱・転倒回復用に温存する。鉄蟲糸技だけでなく機動力確保に使う。",
      "鉄蟲糸技はダメージ以外の固有効果を持つ。状態異常付与（操虫棍）、ダメージバフウィンドウ（スラッシュアックス）、モンスター特殊メカニック発動（ヘビィボウガン）など。コンボ最適化前に武器の鉄蟲糸技の機能を習得する。",
      "百竜夜行はハンターランクに応じて難易度が上がる。波状攻撃開始前に砲撃設備1台と近接設備2台を設置して自動ダメージを最大化する。",
      "サンブレイクでは傀異化研究ポイントが終盤クラフトを制限する。AR 21で解放されるAランク傀異化クエストを優先。傀異化素材のドロップ率が通常の3倍。",
      "ガルクは実質的に第2のハンター。バディ防具画面でガルクにナンベリー・特上ポーション・茶屋チケットを装備させ、狩猟中の受動ヒールと状態異常解除を確保する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Village and Hub Quest Balance",
        "body": "Village quests (single player) unlock story progress and are scaled for solo play. Hub quests (multiplayer) provide better HR progress and rarer material drop rates. Complete Village quests up to 4-star to unlock Wyverian Prints for armour crafting, then switch to Hub quests for primary progression. The Key Monsters for Hub progress are different from Village—always check the Quest Board for Hub Key Monster quests rather than farming non-Key optional quests."
      },
      {
        "title": "Silkbind Upgrade Priority",
        "body": "Each weapon type has three Silkbind attacks: two default and one unlockable via Buddy Dojo and Switch Skills scrolls. The switch skill scroll system unlocks at Hunter Rank 4—prioritise the first scroll (Level 1 Switch Skills) immediately upon unlock. Most meta weapon builds use a mix of default and switched Silkbind attacks; the game does not tell you which combination is optimal. Research your specific weapon on the Rise community database or tier list before spending Followers on experiments."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Follower Quests for Materials",
        "body": "Follower quests (Sunbreak feature) add NPC hunters to your party for specific quests. Follower NPCs never cart, deal approximately 25% of player-level DPS, and provide healing support. Use Follower quests for materials from monsters you find difficult: Follower AI handles repositioning perfectly and creates constant stagger opportunities. The downside is Follower quests do not provide HR experience—alternate between Follower quests for gear and Hub quests for rank advancement."
      },
      {
        "title": "Anomaly Investigations and Crafting",
        "body": "Anomaly Investigations (Sunbreak endgame) are unlocked from AR 1 and scale up to AR 300+. Each investigation provides specific Anomaly materials needed for Qurious Crafting—the augmentation system that adds randomised bonus skills to armour. The optimal Qurious Crafting loop: complete A5 to A10 Investigations for bulk Anomaly Slotting materials → augment high-skill-point armour pieces (5-skill pieces first) → repeat at higher AR tier once the Anomaly Research cap increases."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Qurious Crafting Optimisation",
        "body": "Qurious Crafting randomises bonus skill additions to armour from a pool of valid additions per piece. The critical concept: each piece has a fixed budget (measured in points) and higher-rank skills cost more points. To get a meta bonus (Attack Boost +4 or Weakness Exploit +2 at maximum budget), you need a piece with a high maximum budget rating. Check the Qurious Crafting tool resources to identify which armour pieces have high-budget ceilings before investing materials—low-budget pieces cannot roll the most impactful bonuses regardless of attempts."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Spending Wirebugs on Silkbind attacks when the monster is enraged—enrage reduces Silkbind effectiveness by 30%; save Wirebug charges for repositioning during enrage and use standard combos instead.",
      "Building a full armour set for each new monster—Rise's skill system rewards mixing pieces from different sets; a 2-piece and 3-piece combination from different armours provides more skill slots than any single-monster full set.",
      "Ignoring the Dango meal system—Dango active skills provide passive boosts worth 5–15% effectiveness improvement on specific hunt types; always select Dango appropriate to the monster's element and your weapon type before quests.",
      "Not using the Hunter's Notes for monster weak points—the Hunter's Notes in the menu screen shows exact elemental weakness tiers for every monster. Many Rise monsters have different weaknesses than their World equivalents.",
      "Attempting Sunbreak content with base Rise gear—Sunbreak starts at Master Rank 1 and scales to HR equivalent 200+; enter Sunbreak with full High Rank armour at minimum HR 100 and ideally with 5-piece High Rank set skills active."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "モンスターが怒り状態の時に翔蟲を鉄蟲糸技に使う。怒りは鉄蟲糸技効果を30%低下させる。怒り中は翔蟲チャージを位置調整用に温存し、通常コンボを使う。",
      "新しいモンスターごとにフルセット防具を作る。ライズのスキルシステムは異なるセットのパーツを組み合わせることで報酬が最大化する。2ピース+3ピースの組み合わせは同一モンスターフルセットよりスキルスロットが多い。",
      "団子の食事システムを無視する。団子のアクティブスキルは特定の狩猟タイプで5〜15%の効果向上を提供する。クエスト前にモンスターの属性と武器タイプに合った団子を必ず選ぶ。",
      "狩猟手帳でモンスターの弱点を確認しない。メニュー画面の狩猟手帳は全モンスターの正確な属性弱点を表示する。多くのライズモンスターはワールド版と異なる弱点を持つ。",
      "ベースライズの装備でサンブレイクに入る。サンブレイクはマスターランク1から始まり、HR換算200+まで拡張する。最低HRランク100でフル高レアリティ防具を装備して、可能なら5ピースセットスキル効果を持たせてから入る。"
